{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And He stated the law of the meal-offering.</b> He said that it must all be brought before the altar, for it is to El, blessed be He, alone that the offerer brings his entire offering, and the priests earn their portion from the table of the Most High. And that a small portion of the whole is what is chosen as a pleasing fragrance, and that the priests' portion also makes atonement and is guarded against leavening just like the portion of the Most High. And that the priest's meal-offering belongs entirely to the Most High — not merely a small portion of it as with the meal-offering of the congregation."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:35:51.730200357Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}